To check the sheaf property for a covering $\{ V_ i \to V\} _{i \in I}$ first consider the Čech fppf hypercovering $a : V_\bullet \to V$ with $V_ n = \coprod _{i_0 \ldots i_ n} V_{i_0} \times _ V \ldots \times _ V V_{i_ n}$ and then set $U_\bullet = V_\bullet \times _{a, V} X_ V$. Then $U_\bullet \to X_ V$ is an fppf hypercovering to which we may apply Simplicial Spaces, Lemma <a href="/tag/0DL9" data-tag="0DL9">85.35.1</a>.